            %p
              Conversely, for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt 0
              the real part of the integrand decays as the
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negative+number"} negative
              imaginary part increases, and hence in this case the given line integral equals the contour integral for a contour
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi C
                      %mo −
                    %mo ⊂
                    %mi ℂ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_- \subset \mathbb{C}
              closing in the lower half plane. Since the integrand has no pole in the lower half plane, in this case the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cauchy+integral+formula"} Cauchy integral formula
              says that this integral is zero.
          %p
            Conversely, by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+inversion+theorem"} Fourier inversion theorem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform"} Fourier transform
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heaviside+distribution"} Heaviside distribution
            is the Cauchy principal value as in prop.
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#CauchyPrincipalValueEqualsIntegrationWithImaginaryOffsetPlusDelta"}
          #RelationToFourierTransformOfHeavisideDistribution.num_example
            %h6#example_4 Example
            %p
              %strong
                (relation to
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Fourier+transform"} Fourier transform
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heaviside+distribution"} Heaviside distribution
                \/
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Schwinger+parameter"} Schwinger parameterization
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mi Θ
                              %mo ^
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
